DEPENDENCY DEFERRAL — why the two xcodebuild scheme steps are DEFERRED (not green)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
REPRODUCED (not assumed). Building the app target on this host fails deterministically:

  $ xcodebuild -project TeslaSync.xcodeproj -target TeslaSync -sdk iphonesimulator build
  error: There is no XCFramework found at
         '.../apps/apple/Frameworks/Shared.xcframework'. (in target 'TeslaSync')
  ** BUILD FAILED **
  BUILD_RESULT=65

The TeslaSync iOS/macOS app targets link the KMP `Shared.xcframework` (ADR-004). Staging it
requires the Kotlin/Native Apple toolchain via `apps/shared/gradlew :core:assembleSharedXCFramework`
(a scheme pre-build phase). `apps/macos-pending-verifications.md` defers this artifact to the
`macos-latest` CI runners (origin S3-0001 → H8-0001 / P99-0001). Additionally this host has NO iOS
Simulator runtime installed (xcrun simctl lists no iPhone 16 / no iOS runtime; only iOS 26.5 /
macOS 26.5 SDK headers), so the named `-destination 'platform=iOS Simulator,name=iPhone 16'` is
unavailable regardless. Both are pre-existing environment/integration dependencies OUTSIDE this
surface's allowed file scope (CostForecastWidget.* + this log) — NOT a defect in this surface, and
not stage-able without editing forbidden paths.

Scope note: `struct DashboardWidgetSize` / `DashboardWidgetRegistration` is defined exactly ONCE
(Sources/DashboardWidgets/DashboardWidgetInfra.swift); CostForecastWidget.* adds no redefinition.
Per project.yml the co-located *Tests.swift are excluded from the app target and compiled only into
the XCTest bundles, so they introduce no app-target import of XCTest.

Net: the full-app `xcodebuild build test` is DEFERRED to the signed macos-latest acceptance gate
(P99-0001), matching the disposition of every sibling P4 dashboard-widget surface. The surface
itself is proven GREEN by [A]/[B]/[C]/[D] against the real design system + Swift 6 strict concurrency.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY NOTES (documented, not silent — covenant rule 9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  • Data/composition/states reproduced from the web source: vehicle resolution (vehicleId ??
    vehicles[0].id) lives in the P1/S8 source; the view binds CostForecastModel only — NO HTTP.
  • buildChartData ported verbatim: [...historical(isForecast:false), ...forecast(isForecast:true)]
    .slice(-6); nextCost = forecast[0].cost ?? 0; lastCost = historical.last.cost ?? 0;
    trendUp = nextCost >= lastCost. Stat strings via formatCurrency(…, 0/2) exactly as the web.
  • Compact (cols<=1) = the two-stat row (Next Month, Trend), no chart — web isCompact branch.
    Standard (cols>=2) = three-stat header (Next Month, Avg $/kWh, Trend) + bar chart. isWide
    (cols>=3) enlarges the axis font (web axisTick vs axisTickSm).
  • Bar color: the web fills every bar one indigo (#6366f1). The native chart keeps that hue but
    renders the PROJECTED (forecast) months at reduced opacity vs the RECORDED (historical) months
    — a faithful rendering of the isForecast flag already in the web BarDatum and the idiomatic cue
    for a forecast chart. The chart's VoiceOver value names the recent-vs-projected split so the
    same context reaches screen-reader users. No new user-facing string; documented here so it is
    not silent drift.

